{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519299-my-contagion-chronicle-idea","id":1519299,"title":"My Contagion Chronicle Idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-31T18:13:56-07:00","id":1519299,"title":"My Contagion Chronicle Idea","content":"(NOTE: This idea was originally posted on a discord server so the formatting will look weird)<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve finally made a contagion chronicles outline! Mainly for a group of a human, vampire, Deviant and werewolf (with a Demon cell of 4 as supporting characters)<br /> <br /> so yeah, let me know how you all like this idea.<br /> <br /> edit: (Also\u2026. My original idea is using this for a fanfic-story, but I worked hard on it and thought I\u2019d share)<br /> <br /> <b>IDEA: </b>The GodMachine creates infected Elimination infrastructure. Like a big factory or a power plant. (Going to go with power plant) It creates a thick fog (use *Heavy Rain* or *Blizzard* environmental conditions for sight and perception penalties). It takes dead or near-dead bodies from the hospital and transports them to the structure. There, they get tossed into an incinerator (the lynchpin) and it bellows out the fog. Problem is, it\u2019s STUCK on \u2018make fog\u2019. Maybe the fog is combustible via something in the power plant, or another infrastructure\u2026 point is, the fog is continuing to spread. What happens when the right \u2018match\u2019 is struck in this theoretically-flammable fog? (That\u2019s up to you)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SYMPTOMS OF CONTAGION:</b><br /> <br /> 1. Fog continues to billow into town and surrounding areas in a perfect radius. And it blocks out the sun to the point of being stuck at being no brighter than \u2018dusk\u2019.<br /> <br /> 2. The fog has a red tint and carries Vitae and Essence (and maybe Aether). *<i>Provides a +1 temporary point. Once a day*</i><br /> <br /> 3. The edge of the fog is where it\u2019s the thickest. Driving and hiking through it is a chance-die (at least for the NPCs) to get through. Failure means you end up coming out a totally different inside edge. *(<i>ex: head out north, fail roll, you come into the edge on the south.)*</i>. Dramatic fail could mean a loss of integrity or kidnapped by angels (see **characters** 3a) or something else.<br /> <br /> <b>CONSEQUENCES</b><br /> <br /> 1a. Spirits and monsters become more common. They start stalking the streets.<br /> <br /> 1B. Further out past the city limits, the fog gets thicker. Easier to get lost and better to hide illicit activities.<br /> <br /> 2A. Something in the Vitae in the air is *<i>off</i>.*. Vampires are easier to enrage and harder to calm down.<br /> (+/-1 to appropriate rolls)<br /> <br /> 2b. Harmony is disrupted for werewolves. The fog can boost it or drain it each day. *<i>(At beginning of \u2018day\u2019 roll 1d10: 1-4: -1 harmony, 5-6: no change, 7-10: +1 Harmony)*</i><br /> <br /> <br /> 3a. There\u2019s ONE thing that comes through. A train. A large cargo train. People hear it come in, goods show up, and it leaves. NOBODY remembers it having a loading crew or anything. Just train shows up, delivery trucks mysteriously filled, ready for humans or undercover angels or others to drive to the stores or warehouse/s. But the train station runs close to the power plant, doubling as a Defense Infrastructure for the power plant. (Only way I could think of to keep the mortals from just up and leaving the town while still keeping them healthy)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>CHARACTERS</b><br /> 1a. Cultists of the GM, or another organization, start making problems. But the chief of police can\u2019t do much because he\u2019s running a bit thin, especially with other problems.<br /> <br /> 1B. A friend of the Deviant has tracked the conspiracy (the WF) to the outskirts of town, where some civilians (or supernaturals) are kidnapped or lured for experiments or to boost the new militia. (See **<b>COMPLICATIONS</b>** 1a and 1B)<br /> <br /> 2A. Due to the frenzy and/or drunk on the bonus vitae (and being able to walk in \u2018the day\u2019), some vampires have battled on others territories. Less secrecy and planning, more slaughter.<br /> <br /> 2b. The werewolves can get a bit more savage, also thinking themselves more powerful. Some succumb to their wolves, starting fights with other tribes (or even with the vampires). Others try to retreat deeper into the nearby woods or hide in the city.<br /> <br /> 3a. Due to it being defensive infrastructure, Angels and their kind won\u2019t allow anyone unauthorized (ie; the delivery/cargo truck drivers) onto the property. The drivers themselves are even limited to just the area with their trucks.<br /> <br /> **<b>COMPLICATIONS</b>:** (this is where my ideas start blending in with one another)<br /> <br /> 1a. Contacts and allies are less helpful in the police department. Chief is even ORDERED to relax on missing persons cases by the deviant\u2019s conspiracy.<br /> *<i>(-1 to rolls dealing with most police and aid social rolls)</i>*<br /> <br /> 1B. Deviant\u2019s conspiracy has taken up arms as a \u2018heroic militia\u2019 or \u2018PMC of the people\u2019. While also going to eliminate the supernatural, they also try to find the escaped Deviant. And to do experiments on other people.<br /> *<i>(Conspiracy agents patrolling the streets and will shoot first if the heroes are too close to some places they shouldn\u2019t be. Maybe some are corrupted god machine agents?)</i>*<br /> <br /> 2A. The vampires target the homeless, people they secretly hate and even criminals. Maybe some of the vampires work with/for criminals? The black market and underground networks, even the bars and clubs are paranoid or closed. What vampires are still sane retreat into dens or homes<br /> *(<i>Vampires could ambush the PCs, and/or limit the contact they have with shady individuals)*</i><br /> <br /> 2B. Similar to the vampires. Hunt people they hate, cause terror for hikers and campers, stories of \u2018mad dog things\u2019. Those that HAVENT gone insane in frenzy are starting to go insane from being confined to human and near-human forms. If someone sees them, they\u2019ll get shot or reported.<br /> *(<i>Werewolf contacts and tribes are wary of the pack member)</i>*<br /> <br /> 3a. The corrupted angels will not allow anyone into the power plant that\u2019s causing this whole mess. Some angels could even HIDE *<i>IN</i>* the fog, kidnapping people and other supernaturals to add to the fog machine. And since the train station and train are defense infrastructures, that\u2019s just ANOTHER level of \u2018oh shit\u2019 to deal with.<br /> *(<i>Very difficult to assault the power plant. No plans exist of it, or at least none that can be understood)</i>*<br /> <br /> 3Ai. If anyone does manage to get on the train, when it reaches the edge of the fog, they\u2019ll just \u2018emerge\u2019 in the power plant.<br /> <i>(Basically an easy way to A: keep the NPCs from leaving and B: keep fueling the broken machine)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and the 4 demons? They\u2019re sent to stop the infrastructure, but they MIGHT get spotted unusually easy if they tried to do this themselves. (Idk)<br /> <br /> <br /> So yeah. I guess what just spawned is a ME3 \u201carmy builder\u201d of sorts. At least from where I\u2019m looking. Either assist, intimidate and/or eliminate the various groups in order to get factions to help you make this INSANE attack on two infrastructure in a single \u2018chapter\u2019/\u2018day\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably some few \u2018down and dirty\u2019 rolls needed. Idk. Or maybe there\u2019s \u201chalf-angel supernaturals\u201d. Like a werewolf with angel-powers?<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming everyone can get inside and destroy the linchpin of the power plant, time kinda \u2018rewinds\u2019 a bit. Maybe the fog gets sucked back into the structure and with it the various things that have occurred. People sacrificed to the infrastructure will remain dead of course, or maybe everyone will wake up like it was a very weird dream.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28143,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","user":"firestar001","date":". 08-01-2023, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T00:32:10-07:00","id":1519319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519299-my-contagion-chronicle-idea#post1519299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(NOTE: This idea was originally posted on a discord server so the formatting will look weird)<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve finally made a contagion chronicles outline! Mainly for a group of a human, vampire, Deviant and werewolf (with a Demon cell of 4 as supporting characters)<br /> <br /> so yeah, let me know how you all like this idea.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>How you balance them out with each other? Why do these characters associate with each other in the first place? Are you going to give the players pre-made characters that already fit together or is that something to work together into as the players each come up with their character ideas?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519299-my-contagion-chronicle-idea#post1519299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>IDEA: </b>The GodMachine creates infected Elimination infrastructure. Like a big factory or a power plant. (Going to go with power plant) It creates a thick fog (use *Heavy Rain* or *Blizzard* environmental conditions for sight and perception penalties). It takes dead or near-dead bodies from the hospital and transports them to the structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't <b>vampires </b>also count as &quot;dead or near-dead bodies&quot; to be taken? Or maybe the &quot;Fog Plant's&quot; criteria for &quot;materials for processing&quot; only counts <i>inanimate/not moving</i> bodies (meaning vampires are out, but comatose people or things that look human but are not, like maniquins or statues are also in) as valid or does it only restrict itself to the local hospitals &amp; morgues as extraction places? Would animal carcasses count as an alternate source of materials?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519299-my-contagion-chronicle-idea#post1519299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There, they get tossed into an incinerator (the lynchpin) and it bellows out the fog. Problem is, it\u2019s STUCK on \u2018make fog\u2019. Maybe the fog is combustible via something in the power plant, or another infrastructure\u2026 point is, the fog is continuing to spread. What happens when the right \u2018match\u2019 is struck in this theoretically-flammable fog? (That\u2019s up to you)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon the ignorance since it has been years since i last messed with the God-Machine Chronicle or Demon materials, but what is special about Elimination infrastructure and <i><b>infected </b></i>Elimination infrastructure in particular (when compared to other possible types of Infrastructure)?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, how would anyone find out the fog is potentially flammable in the first place without large chunks of the place, Infrastructure included, going kaboom?<br /> Truth be told, i'm not sure it's even necessary in the first place - memes about the British Isles or Alaska notwithstanding, human beings in general are <b>not</b> into living under downcast skies and mist 24/7. If there are no climatic factors to make it &quot;feel&quot; kind of expected, after a few hours a number of people will either start calling the authorities or start to gather and move out of the city under suspicions of either a major fire, a chemical accident or some other form of natural or manmade disaster. Human beings are as capable of panicking and starting a stampede as any herd animal under the right/wrong circunstances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>firestar001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519299-my-contagion-chronicle-idea#post1519299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>SYMPTOMS OF CONTAGION:</b><br /> <br /> 1. Fog continues to billow into town and surrounding areas in a perfect radius. And it blocks out the sun to the point of being stuck at being no brighter than \u2018dusk\u2019.<br /> <br /> 3. The edge of the fog is where it\u2019s the thickest. Driving and hiking through it is a chance-die (at least for the NPCs) to get through. Failure means you end up coming out a totally different inside edge. *(<i>ex: head out north, fail roll, you come into the edge on the south.)*</i>. Dramatic fail could mean a loss of integrity or kidnapped by angels (see **characters** 3a) or something else.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> One problem i see with these two things is that they can potentially make it ridiculously easy to pinpoint the heart of the problem without even trying, since the &quot;Fog Plant&quot; is not only at the center of the fog's <b>perfect</b> circular radius, but also the part of the town/city where it's the thinnest, read, it's literally <b><i>the most clearly visible landmark in the whole region</i></b> since the fog started. It would logically attract even people with zero suspicions, since it's the first thing a person will see amidst the whole mess.<br /> <br /> As an aside, i would suggest - supposing you are not already familiar with either of these works) - taking a look into Stephen King's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mist_(novella)\" target=\"_blank\">the Mist</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Dome_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Under the Dome</a> novels, plus similarly themed classic Carpenter film <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fog\" target=\"_blank\">the Fog</a>. Wait, wait, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_of_Darkness_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a> too, it's very God-Machine-esque in concepts and imagery i'd say.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just my initial thoughts. Going to chime in with more comments or ideas on the rest of your post later. Hope it helps.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-01-2023, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T07:12:39-07:00","id":1519340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519299-my-contagion-chronicle-idea?p=1519319#post1519319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How you balance them out with each other? Why do these characters associate with each other in the first place? Are you going to give the players pre-made characters that already fit together or is that something to work together into as the players each come up with their character ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't really need to balance them with one another, let them all be good at different things and let them shine when their thing comes up. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One problem i see with these two things is that they can potentially make it ridiculously easy to pinpoint the heart of the problem without even trying, since the &quot;Fog Plant&quot; is not only at the center of the fog's <b>perfect</b> circular radius, but also the part of the town/city where it's the thinnest, read, it's literally <b><i>the most clearly visible landmark in the whole region</i></b> since the fog started. It would logically attract even people with zero suspicions, since it's the first thing a person will see amidst the whole mess. </div> </div> </div>When was the last time you or anyone you knew tried to find the center of a patch of fog? <br /> <br /> That aside, I would have the fog at least partially subject to local weather patterns, that way you can have it eb and flow. I think that would make a better atmosphere, IMO. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> --------------<br /> <br /> I've only partially cinsidered OP's post but I do want to mention I don't think I would add or subtract harmony from the Uratha. I think I would adjust the gauntlet. Gives a good reason for increased spirit activity on days it is lowered and makes spirits more desperate on days it is raised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T15:15:12-07:00","id":1519370,"title":"","content":"I have two pieces of advice on this idea.<br /> First, create a degree of seperation between the plant and the fog. Instead of having it spew the fog from its smokestakes have it secretly dumping contaminants into a large swamp which then produces the fog or place natural caverns or abandoned mine tunnels underneath the area with polutants dumped within slowly seeping out through the ground. This slows any actaul action against the plant. Sure some people will immediately blame it but the powers that be will seek evidence before rocking that boat.<br /> As for the perfect circle idea, use local geography to control the fogs spread while hidding its origin. Fog settles in low areas so place your community in a valley or series of hollows.<br /> <br /> Second, as far as keeping people from fleeing the area, don't. Unless this goes on for years few people will abandon their homes and jobs to move away. Let life go on as normal for most people, at least for a while, they just have to look away occasionaly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T15:48:59-07:00","id":1519373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1519299-my-contagion-chronicle-idea?p=1519319#post1519319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How you balance them out with each other? Why do these characters associate with each other in the first place? Are you going to give the players pre-made characters that already fit together or is that something to work together into as the players each come up with their character ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s just it. You don\u2019t. (I kid you not that\u2019s what the book says. Like a mummy vs hunter, 1v1, mummy is gonna win.)<br /> the book does say to give players moments to shine. As for the association; I got some \u2018prologue\u2019 ideas that will send them all to a certain location in the city (after encountering their own brands of \u2018weirdness\u2019) and someone/thing basically saying \u201cyou aren\u2019t crazy. Things are happening.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wouldn't <b>vampires </b>also count as &quot;dead or near-dead bodies&quot; to be taken? Or maybe the &quot;Fog Plant's&quot; criteria for &quot;materials for processing&quot; only counts <i>inanimate/not moving</i> bodies (meaning vampires are out, but comatose people or things that look human but are not, like maniquins or statues are also in) as valid or does it only restrict itself to the local hospitals &amp; morgues as extraction places? Would animal carcasses count as an alternate source of materials? </div> </div> </div>My notes say the red-fog holds Vitae in it, and also say Angels also kidnap supernatural creatures. The requirement is mostly \u2018needs to have blood\u2019. <br /> (notes for the vampire prologue say Angels are robbing from vampire-owned blood banks)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pardon the ignorance since it has been years since i last messed with the God-Machine Chronicle or Demon materials, but what is special about Elimination infrastructure and <i><b>infected </b></i>Elimination infrastructure in particular (when compared to other possible types of Infrastructure)? </div> </div> </div>Elimination infrastructure, as far as I can understand, is supposed to \u2018eliminate evidence it was there\u2019 or be a \u2018kill box\u2019. Or, as Flowers of Hell says, it also \u201ctidies up\u201d after a project. <br /> <br /> the \u201cInfected\u201d part is important because the infrastructure isn\u2019t doing what it\u2019s supposed to. It\u2019s like a program that\u2019s frozen on a certain step, or it\u2019s on loop. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how would anyone find out the fog is potentially flammable in the first place without large chunks of the place, Infrastructure included, going kaboom? </div> </div> </div>That part is probably never going to come up, or if the players/characters need extra motivation. And it\u2019s not flammable in the traditional sense. So people can still use flamethrowers without blowing it up. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Truth be told, i'm not sure it's even necessary in the first place - memes about the British Isles or Alaska notwithstanding, human beings in general are <b>not</b> into living under downcast skies and mist 24/7. If there are no climatic factors to make it &quot;feel&quot; kind of expected, after a few hours a number of people will either start calling the authorities or start to gather and move out of the city under suspicions of either a major fire, a chemical accident or some other form of natural or manmade disaster. Human beings are as capable of panicking and starting a stampede as any herd animal under the right/wrong circunstances. </div> </div> </div>I got the idea from an episode of Forensic Files. There was this HUGE wreck on a bridge during a sudden fog, only the fog was caused by some factory (with weather and wind contributing to it)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One problem i see with these two things is that they can potentially make it ridiculously easy to pinpoint the heart of the problem without even trying, since the &quot;Fog Plant&quot; is not only at the center of the fog's <b>perfect</b> circular radius, but also the part of the town/city where it's the thinnest, read, it's literally <b><i>the most clearly visible landmark in the whole region</i></b> since the fog started. It would logically attract even people with zero suspicions, since it's the first thing a person will see amidst the whole mess. </div> </div> </div>Earlier drafts of this involved taking the whole town \u2018out of time\u2019 or something equally crazy and dr who-ish. <br /> Again, looking back at my notes, while the fog WOULD be thinnest at the power plant, there\u2019s the fact that the road UP TO the plant is effectively blocked off thanks to the Angels and Cultists. So nobody would even be able to tell it\u2019s thinner. While WE know the fog is \u201cthin, normal, thick, thicc\u201d, the NPCs and PCs just know \u201cit\u2019s f**king hard to see\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside, i would suggest - supposing you are not already familiar with either of these works) - taking a look into Stephen King's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Mist_(novella)\" target=\"_blank\">the Mist</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Under_the_Dome_(novel)\" target=\"_blank\">Under the Dome</a> novels, plus similarly themed classic Carpenter film <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Fog\" target=\"_blank\">the Fog</a>. Wait, wait, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince_of_Darkness_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">this one</a> too, it's very God-Machine-esque in concepts and imagery i'd say.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just my initial thoughts. Going to chime in with more comments or ideas on the rest of your post later. Hope it helps.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I hope I answered all your questions. And, I\u2019ll admit I made this contagion mainly so I can write a fanfic, but thought I could at least SHARE the design. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28143-firestar001","name":"firestar001","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}